From b93028d6307f466762ef6e3963e245d9d1a66c9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:07:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 203/206] [vm] Pin G1/G4 acceptance state (2026-10-16..19)

Working-tree changes accumulated while closing G1 (option/fixture parity)
and G4 (malformed-patch handling), committed together so device and
host evidence can name one SDK revision.

G1:
- precompiler: reorder the global object pool by the
  --base_op_link_data mapping after renumbering pool accesses, and print
  "Sorted ObjectPool, moved N of M entries." (RC8/RC12).
- linker/precompiler: DD voting tallies all votes and picks the winner in
  hash-table order; ScoreVoter checks the target before the caller; the
  first ResolveDDSlots pass runs before DispatchTableGenerator::Initialize
  (RC9).
- JIT: object-pool load padding, Thread-offset lazy native dispatch, the
  is_simulating guard for leaf runtime calls, the native-entry Thread
  offsets in the kFullJIT features string, and a deserialization reset for
  linked trampolines (RC11).
- analyze_snapshot: load_obfuscation_map coverage (RC7) and related
  dump fixes.

G4:
- elf_loader: reject bad magic, out-of-file segments, p_filesz > p_memsz
  and address overflow instead of crashing.
- app_snapshot: drop the WrapCode RELEASE_ASSERT that compared ELF patch
  bytes with the Mach-O base; the simulator runs the patch's own bytes.
- Dart_SnapshotDataSize: include the Shorebird extra block that follows
  the snapshot at the next 64-byte boundary. Shorebird's public engine
  passes this size straight to the updater's base stream, and patches are
  diffed against --dump_blobs, which counts that block.

Tests: wrapper_stub_test Resume count, dd_voting_test, link_info_test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

